      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To help the procurement team identify \"high-intensity\" or \"unpredictable\" creators, consider the following behavioral and linguistic \"red flag\" indicators:\n\nBehavioral:\n\n- Excessive hand gestures or body language, such as rapid waving, pointing, or flailing\n- Loud or aggressive tone, including yelling, screaming, or using a confrontational inflection\n- Fidgeting, tapping, or other signs of nervous energy\n- Overuse of filler words (e.g., \"um,\" \"ah,\" \"you know\") or hesitation in speech\n- Abrupt or jerky movements, such as sudden changes in camera angle or pace\n- Display of intense emotions, such as rage, excitement, or despair, in a way that may be perceived as unprofessional\n\nLinguistic:\n\n- Overuse of slang, jargon, or colloquialisms that may be perceived as unrefined or common\n- Use of aggressive or confrontational language, including profanity or derogatory terms\n- Rapid-fire speech or a tendency to ramble or speak in a disjointed manner\n- Overuse of rhetorical questions or emotive language, such as \"What's wrong with you people?\" or \"Don't you know what's going",
